Z||000000||theogre||12-16-2000||08:17 PM||||Like many of you I've been having problems with my OE radio. so today I pulled it out to have a look. I found a few things other than the belt that will make the them do queer things. (I'll do a better writup next week.)<P><B>Clicking or poping noises from the tape deck.</B><P>Check the gear teeth on the flywheels and other things. They get junk jammed in there and click/pop as they hit the lumps.<P>This is a little tricky because you have to carefully pull the flywheel/capstan out off its bearing. There is a spring washer and a plastic washer on each capstan. When you pull it out make sure you don't loose these. When putting it back together make sure the spring is sharp side toward the flywheel and the washer goes on after the spring. If you get this wrong it will screw up the bearing.<P>|F||L|----)---|--<BR>|Y|<BR>-spring^---^washer<P>Also if the capstans won't come out scrape the crud off them with a finger nail or wood stick. Don't force them or you could make the bearing bind. That junk on the capstan is abrasive.<P>Warning: if you take out the screw that holds the cassette drive spindles make sure you keep track of it. This screw is shorter than the 3 that hold the plate over the flywheels.<P>All you who are doing the belt thing should check those gears at the same time.<P><B>Main power/speeker connector</B><P>The solder joints crack where the connector is soldered to a little board. You have to take off the top cover, side bracket, and all the screws holding the finned heatsink. Then you can carefully rework the connector.<P>This problem can cause loose connections that make you think speakers are bad. It can also make the display go dead when you put the parking lights on.<P><B>Display dead.</B><P>check the small 2 wire connector. If that's unplugged or loose the display won't come on at all.<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||165.121.88.242||reg||7
